{
  "text": " I worked as a director of rehab for five months at another skilled nursing facility here in Kalihi, Anahu, and at that facility during my time as being the director of rehab, I seen where the billing department would have my therapist change the ICD-10 medical diagnosis billing code from pulmonary disorder or COPD to COVID because of higher reimbursement. Now these people were asymptomatic, some of them may have had a positive PCR and some of them didn't have a positive PCR test, but we were still forced to change those ICD-10 diagnosis codes to a COVID code because we get higher reimbursement for those patients. So it's just fraud on every level, just higher reimbursement in medical facilities for someone that's labeled COVID. Whether you treat them for COVID or not, you're going to get higher reimbursement. I know this for a fact.",
